cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SeedBox, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "SeedBox: A user-friendly software package for high-throughput seed morphometry modelling for quantitative plant ecology"
version: "2.01"
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Montcharles/SeedBox"
url: "https://github.com/Montcharles/SeedBox"
abstract: >-
  SeedBox: Dimensional Morphometry is academic software for the dimensional
  morphometry of seeds. From three linear measurements of each seed (length,
  width and thickness) it computes the derived physical properties, compares
  treatments or populations, describes the multivariate structure of the data
  and uses machine learning to assess how well the seed lots can be told apart.
keywords:
  - seed morphometry
  - seed dimensions
  - physical properties of seeds
  - plant ecology
  - machine learning
  - self-organizing map
